CD-ROM drives: a disc changed while the PC runs, as a real drive.
- An empty drive: an image name of "" (ide_attach_cd), or the disc taken out (ide_change_cd with "").
- No disc: TEST UNIT READY and reads answer "medium not present" (a read had gone to no file).
- ide_change_cd reports a failed change (the image doesn't open: the old disc stays, the guest isn't told).
- The UNIT ATTENTION after a change is reported once, then commands go on: it had held every command
  until a REQUEST SENSE, which FreeDOS's UDVD2 never sends (the drive stayed "not ready" for good).

